1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,337
PayFence reviews contractor invoices before signing an E V M

2
00:00:03,337 --> 00:00:06,525
payment. This recording uses the working local application, sample invoices,

3
00:00:06,525 --> 00:00:09,713
and an automated test wallet. Every contract transaction uses valueless

4
00:00:09,713 --> 00:00:12,901
mock tokens on an ephemeral local chain.

5
00:00:14,202 --> 00:00:16,797
Studio North's invoice requests a different wallet from the registered

6
00:00:16,797 --> 00:00:19,392
vendor. The recipient check fails, and approval is disabled. The

7
00:00:19,392 --> 00:00:21,987
familiar vendor name does not override the exact destination being

8
00:00:21,987 --> 00:00:24,582
requested.

9
00:00:25,895 --> 00:00:29,038
Restoring the registered wallet resolves this sample exception. The review

10
00:00:29,038 --> 00:00:32,182
also checks duplicate invoice references, the vendor's per payment limit,

11
00:00:32,182 --> 00:00:35,325
and a valid nonzero destination. These are specific controls, not

12
00:00:35,325 --> 00:00:38,468
a guarantee against every kind of fraud.

13
00:00:39,771 --> 00:00:42,650
The reviewer can now approve the current invoice details. PayFence

14
00:00:42,650 --> 00:00:45,529
stores an approval fingerprint. This dashboard approval is a review

15
00:00:45,529 --> 00:00:48,409
decision, not a wallet signature or a blockchain payment.

16
00:00:49,719 --> 00:00:52,314
Now the amount changes. Saving the edit increments the revision,

17
00:00:52,314 --> 00:00:54,909
clears the old approval, and returns the invoice to review.

18
00:00:54,909 --> 00:00:57,504
This prevents the dashboard from presenting an earlier approval as

19
00:00:57,504 --> 00:01:00,098
approval of changed details.

20
00:01:01,404 --> 00:01:04,328
After reviewing the new amount, the invoice is approved again.

21
00:01:04,328 --> 00:01:07,252
The downloaded review packet includes the checks, revision, approval match,

22
00:01:07,252 --> 00:01:10,176
audit result, and a packet hash. It is portable review

23
00:01:10,176 --> 00:01:13,101
evidence, not proof that money has moved.

24
00:01:14,409 --> 00:01:17,685
The audit trail records recipient restoration, approval, and the later

25
00:01:17,685 --> 00:01:20,961
edit. Integrity verification checks the hashes and links. A separately

26
00:01:20,961 --> 00:01:24,236
retained head can detect truncation; the chain does not prove

27
00:01:24,236 --> 00:01:27,512
authorship or prevent an administrator from rewriting the whole history.

28
00:01:28,815 --> 00:01:31,255
The signed payment lab selects the approved invoice. This automated

29
00:01:31,255 --> 00:01:33,694
test wallet deploys a valueless mock token and the PayFence

30
00:01:33,694 --> 00:01:36,134
contract on local chain thirty one thousand three hundred thirty

31
00:01:36,134 --> 00:01:38,574
seven. No public deployment or human wallet extension is being

32
00:01:38,574 --> 00:01:41,014
claimed.

33
00:01:42,317 --> 00:01:45,215
The lab registers the invoice vendor, mints test tokens, grants

34
00:01:45,215 --> 00:01:48,112
the exact allowance, signs the order, and executes it. The

35
00:01:48,112 --> 00:01:51,009
contract checks the recipient, amount limit, payer signature, expiry, and

36
00:01:51,009 --> 00:01:53,906
invoice replay marker. The app rechecks the current approval before

37
00:01:53,906 --> 00:01:56,803
signing and sending.

38
00:01:58,120 --> 00:02:01,673
The receipt confirms a real local contract transaction to the

39
00:02:01,673 --> 00:02:05,226
invoice recipient. The signed evidence includes the domain, order, signature,

40
00:02:05,226 --> 00:02:08,779
transaction hash, and block number. Dashboard status remains separate, so

41
00:02:08,779 --> 00:02:12,332
this prototype does not claim automatic settlement reconciliation.

42
00:02:13,642 --> 00:02:16,119
The optional M C P service exposes three read only

43
00:02:16,119 --> 00:02:18,596
tools: review the queue, prepare a review packet, and verify

44
00:02:18,596 --> 00:02:21,073
the audit. Here are actual S D K responses from

45
00:02:21,073 --> 00:02:23,550
an exported workspace snapshot. The service cannot approve an invoice

46
00:02:23,550 --> 00:02:26,027
or send funds.

47
00:02:27,340 --> 00:02:31,136
PayFence connects invoice checks to exact authorization and inspectable evidence.

48
00:02:31,136 --> 00:02:34,932
The local app, contract flow, and review tools work. Customer

49
00:02:34,932 --> 00:02:38,728
validation, public Sepolia proof, and production controls remain next steps.

50
00:02:38,728 --> 00:02:42,524
No real stablecoin settlement or customer traction is claimed.
